      "math_academy_id": "e-6710",
      "problem": "Given that  $(3s^2 + 2s - 1)(s^2 + s + 2) = 3s^4 + \\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{a}s^3 + \\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{b}s^2 + \\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{c}s - 2,$ calculate $a+b+c.$",
      "worked_solution": "We distribute all three terms of the trinomial in the first set of parentheses to the trinomial in the second set of parentheses. Then, we simplify.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3{s}^{2}+2s-1)({s}^{2}+s+2) & = \\\\ 3{s}^{2}({s}^{2}+s+2)+2s({s}^{2}+s+2)+(-1)({s}^{2}+s+2) & = \\\\ 3{s}^{4}+3{s}^{3}+6{s}^{2}+2{s}^{3}+2{s}^{2}+4s-{s}^{2}-s-2 & = \\\\ 3{s}^{4}+5{s}^{3}+7{s}^{2}+3s-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMatching up the coefficients, we find that $a=5,$ $b=7,$ and $c=3.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\na + b + c = 5 + 7 + 3 = 15.\n$$",
